odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41120-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41121:20.404 style:writing-mode
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41122-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41123-20.404.1 General
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41124-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41125:The style:writing-mode attribute controls the direction in which characters are ordered within a line (inline direction), the direction in which lines are stacked (block direction) and the glyph orientation of individual characters. Furthermore it controls the order and display direction of columns in layout objects like section, table or page and in text boxes (called here layout direction).
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41126-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41127-Note: In context of these sections, the term “character” is to be interpreted to mean a text character as perceived by the user, or a glyph as defined in Unicode. 
--
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41129-The orientation of images and shapes is not affected by the writing mode.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41130-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41131:The defined values for the style:writing-mode attribute are lr-tb, lr, rl-tb, rl, tb-rl, tb, tb-lr, sideways-rl, sideways-lr and page. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41132-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41133-•lr-tb: see §7.27.7 of [XSL]. 
--
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41187-•page: This value specifies that the writing-mode is inherited from the closest layout object in which the element is contained or from the anchor object of the element. Details are specified in the following sections. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41188-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41189:Note: The style:writing-mode attribute can also be used in chart styles. However, it does not belong to the <style:chart-properties> element, but to the <style:graphic-properties> element or to the <style:paragraph-properties> element and therefore ‘chart-properties’ does not have its own section here.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41190-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41191-20.404.2 <style:graphic-properties>
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41192-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41193:The style:writing-mode attribute of a <style:graphic-properties> element specifies the layout direction of columns within text boxes that have the graphic style assigned.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41194-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41195-If the attribute value is page the layout direction of columns within text boxes that are anchored to a page is inherited from the layout direction of the page on which the text box is displayed. For text boxes that have a different anchor type, the layout direction is inherited from the paragraph direction of the paragraph or object that contains the text box.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41196-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41197:If a graphic style is evaluated for the style:writing-mode property of a paragraph as specified in section 16.2, not only the <style:paragraph-properties> element but also the <style:graphic-properties> element is evaluated. If the style:writing-mode attribute is present in both elements, it shall have the same value.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41198-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41199:The style:writing-mode attribute is usable with the following element: <style:graphic-properties> 17.21.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41200-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41201:The values of the style:writing-mode attribute are lr-tb, lr, rl-tb, rl, tb-rl, tb, tb-lr, sideways-rl, sideways-lr or page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41202-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41203:20.404.3 <style:page-layout-properties>
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41204-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41205:The style:writing-mode attribute of a <style:page-layout-properties> element specifies the layout direction of page columns for pages that are formatted using the page style. It further determines the binding edge and progress direction of books, see style:page-usage 19.509 and it determines the writing mode in the inheritance chain of objects, which have a style:writing-mode attribute with value page applied.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41206-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41207-The location of the header area at top of a page and the footer area at bottom of a page is not affected by the writing mode of the page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41208-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41209:The value page shall not be use for a style:writing-mode attribute of a <style:page-layout-properties> element..
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41210-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41211:The style:writing-mode attribute is usable with the following element: <style:page-layout-properties> 17.2.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41212-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41213:The values of the style:writing-mode attribute are lr-tb, lr, rl-tb, rl, tb-rl, tb, tb-lr, sideways-rl, sideways-lr or page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41214-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41215:20.404.4 <style:paragraph-properties>
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41216-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41217:The style:writing-mode attribute of a <style:paragraph-properties> element specifies the inline direction, block direction and character orientation for all paragraphs that have the paragraph style assigned.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41218-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41219:The style:writing-mode attribute specifies for the paragraph the base direction required by the BiDi Algoritm, see BD5 of [[UAX9]].
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41220-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41221-Note: The inline direction determines the location of “start” and “end” of a paragraph. For paragraphs that are contained in lists, it thus specifies where the list numbers and bullets are displayed, for writing mode rl-tb on the right side, for example.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41222-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41223:If a <style:paragraph-property> element is child element of a graphic style that is assigned to a text box, then it specifies the layout direction of columns within the text box as well. In case the style writing-mode attribute is present in the <style:paragraph-properties> child element and in the <style:graphic-properties> child element of the same graphic style, their values shall be identical.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41224-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41225-The value page specifies that the actual value is inherited from the layout direction of the closest layout object in which the paragraph is contained, and which has a layout direction other than page. For a paragraph element, which is direct child element of a shape, the closest layout object is the shape itself.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41226-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41227:Note: If a paragraph style does not contain a style:writing-mode attribute, then the hierarchical style model as specified in section 16.2 is used to determine a value for the writing mode of the element that has the paragraph style applied. That is different from an attribute with value page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41228-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41229:The style:writing-mode attribute is usable with the following element: <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41230-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41231:The values of the style:writing-mode attribute are lr-tb, lr, rl-tb, rl, tb-rl, tb, tb-lr, sideways-rl, sideways-lr or page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41232-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41233-20.404.5 <style:section-properties>
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41234-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41235:The style:writing-mode attribute of a <style:section-properties> element specifies the layout direction of section columns for text sections that have the section style assigned.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41236-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41237:The style:writing-mode attribute is usable with the following element: <style:section-properties> 17.11.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41238-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41239:The values of the style:writing-mode attribute are lr-tb, lr, rl-tb, rl, tb-rl, tb, tb-lr, sideways-rl, sideways-lr or page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41240-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41241-20.404.6 <style:table-cell-properties>
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41242-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41243:The style:writing-mode attribute of a <style:table-cell-properties> element specifies a layout directing for any descendant element of the cell that has a style assigned with writing mode page and for which the table cell is the closest containing layout object on which the layout direction is specified.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41244-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41245-Note: OpenDocument further has the table cell style attribute style:direction 20.263 to specify that characters are vertically stacked but not rotated, and it further has the table cell style attribute style:glyph-orientation-vertical 20.297 to specify, that no characters in a vertical writing mode are rotated.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41246-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41247:The style:writing-mode attribute is usable with the following element: <style:table-cell-properties> 17.18.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41248-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41249:The values of the style:writing-mode attribute are lr-tb, lr, rl-tb, rl, tb-rl, tb, tb-lr, sideways-rl, sideways-lr or page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41250-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41251-20.404.7 <style:table-properties>
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41252-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41253:The style:writing-mode attribute of a <style:table-properties> element specifies the layout direction of table columns for tables that have the table style assigned.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41254-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41255-If the attribute value is page the layout direction is inherited from the layout direction of the closest layout object in which the table is contained, and which has a layout direction other than page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41256-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41257:The style:writing-mode attribute is usable with the following element: <style:table-properties> 17.15.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41258-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41259:The values of the style:writing-mode attribute are lr-tb, lr, rl-tb, rl, tb-rl, tb, tb-lr, sideways-rl, sideways-lr or page.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41260-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41261:20.405 style:writing-mode-automatic
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41262-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41263:The style:writing-mode-automatic attribute specifies whether a consumer may recalculate the writing mode of a paragraph based on its content whenever the content is edited. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41264-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41265:The writing-mode should be specified in a style:writing-mode attribute.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41266-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41267:If the fo:text-align with value start, text alignment can be adapted to the writing mode.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41268-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41269:The defined values for the style:writing-mode-automatic attribute are:
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41270-
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt-41271-•false: consumers should not recalculate writing mode of a paragraph whenever its content is edited. 
